because you don't have a backup kidney,

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.530
so you wanna respect that kidney,

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:05.910
meaning you don't wanna overuse

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.860
non-steroidal anti-inflammatories.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.830
You don't wanna consume
nephrotoxic substances.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:13.080
You wanna make sure that
you're always well hydrated.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:13.913
You feel me?

00:10:13.913 --> 00:10:14.746
- Plus they'll put you

00:10:14.746 --> 00:10:17.070
on one of those organ donor sucker lists.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:19.530
Everybody who wants an eyeball or a spine

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.840
or a vestigial tail will be after you!

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:25.470
- I'm an organ donor, proud
organ donor, why aren't you?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.910
Change your license today.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.070
Can you imagine, you could
be one of the lucky people

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.576
that gets one of my organs?

00:10:30.576 --> 00:10:31.680
Just saying.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.977
That's better than merch.

00:10:32.977 --> 00:10:34.890
"Hey, I got a Doctor Mike shirt."

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:35.977
By the way, you can get those down below.

00:10:35.977 --> 00:10:38.585
"But hey, I got Doctor
Mike's eyeball, I win!"

00:10:38.585 --> 00:10:42.060
- [Dan] They don't tell you
where it came from, do they?

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.610
- Dan, can I have fun with my joke?

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.510
God!

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.980
By the way, I gotta dispel that rumor

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:50.130
that people think that if
they get into an accident

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.810
or they're sick, that if you
go into the emergency room

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:53.070
and they see you're an organ donor,

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.780
they don't take good care of you.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.730
That's absolutely false.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:59.010
Zero have I ever heard
of that, and if I did,

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.110
don't you think I probably
would not make myself

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:01.943
an organ donor?

00:11:01.943 --> 00:11:02.970
- What if instead of donating

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.620
one of my old worn out kidneys,

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:07.560
I gave Grandpa that
artificial kidney I invented.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.060
- Homer, that was just a beer can

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.620
with a whistle glued to it.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:12.439
But remember why you're doing this.

00:11:12.439 --> 00:11:15.660
It's for your father,
the man who raised you

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.533
and nurtured you.

00:11:16.533 --> 00:11:19.350
- It's interesting, when
you get a real transplant,

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:22.110
you end up having to take
immunosuppressant medication

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.150
for the rest of your life, but still,

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:27.540
the evidence looks like
getting the kidney transplant,

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.800
you live a longer life

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.845
than someone who has to undergo dialysis

00:11:30.845 --> 00:11:32.640
multiple days of the week.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.250
And odds are, you'll have
a higher quality of life

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.710
'cause you don't have to
always go for dialysis.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.866
- I love you, son.

00:11:39.866 --> 00:11:41.366
- I love you, Dad.

00:11:42.357 --> 00:11:44.190
- Now don't you fellas worry.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:45.780
This'll all be over.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.520
- What's the name of
Justin Bieber's girlfriend?

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.997
Selena Gomez had a kidney
transplant from her friend, right?

00:11:51.997 --> 00:11:53.040
(crickets chirping)

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.780
- [Dan] It rings a bell.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.880
Also that wasn't like
10 years ago they dated?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.830
- Excuse me, I'm still mourning the loss

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.270
of that relationship.

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.103
- What the?

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.440
We gotta get rid of that window.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.630
- Don't worry about old Grandpa.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.820
I'm going to a better place.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:09.653
- I just don't understand

00:12:09.653 --> 00:12:11.520
why they can't put him on dialysis.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.500
We have a lot of patients
in the United States

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.690
who are considered end
stage renal disease.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:19.650
They go on dialysis and they
don't a typically normal life,

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.627
they have a lower quality of life

00:12:20.627 --> 00:12:23.640
'cause they have to be tied
to the dialysis center,

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.130
but they're alive.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:27.300
- I'm sorry, Dad.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.340
The way I behaved was shameful.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:34.340
I guess fear made me run away,
but love made me come back.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.433
- Bless you, son.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.333
- Now Homer, this may
sting just a tiny bit.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.133
- Oh, son of a.

00:12:46.082 --> 00:12:47.128
(brakes skidding)

00:12:47.128 --> 00:12:49.795
(Homer screams)

00:12:52.456 --> 00:12:53.460
- He's waking up.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.833
- Oh Homey, I'm so glad you're all right.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:57.810
- Hey!

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.940
- While we were setting your broken bones

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.560
and putting your blood back in,

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:04.230
we helped ourselves to a kidney
and gave it to your father.

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:06.405
- You don't help yourself to a kidney.

00:13:06.405 --> 00:13:08.171
You usually have to sign off on that one.

00:13:08.171 --> 00:13:11.310
(Grandpa and Homer exclaiming)

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.300
You know what's pretty dark?

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:15.150
In some countries, they
actually sell organs.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:19.050
That's a well known black
market for organ trade.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.450
- I know you're a little
peeved at Grandpa, Dad,

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.730
but you've done a wonderful thing.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:26.321
- Yes, you've shortened
your life significantly

00:13:26.321 --> 00:13:28.650
so someone else can have a slight...

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.720
- He didn't shorten
his life significantly.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.830
Come on, Marge.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.943
- I don't need two kidneys.

00:13:33.943 --> 00:13:36.783
I have everything I need right here.

00:13:37.723 --> 00:13:38.697
Hmm.

00:13:38.697 --> 00:13:41.221
- Dad, you're tickling me.

00:13:41.221 --> 00:13:42.715
- Here's what happens
when you eat McDonald's

00:13:42.715 --> 00:13:44.970
and only McDonald's for 30 days.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.770
Click here to check
that out, and as always,

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:48.960
stay happy and healthy.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.360
Not while eating McDonald's.

